  "description": "The Atlas contains genuinely sophisticated incentive engineering, and it is worth reading together: a revenue-share clock that stops when activity falls below a floor so the gate cannot become the esc",
  "orientation": "The Atlas contains genuinely sophisticated incentive engineering, and it is worth reading together: a revenue-share clock that stops when activity falls below a floor so the gate cannot become the escape hatch; an airdrop formula that deducts collateralized supply so circular loops net to zero and self-updates when risk parameters change; a permissionless kill switch that is cheap to trigger and expensive to reset; and a 100% capital charge used instead of a prohibition where the acting party is outside Sky's authority.",
